r.cs:31`), which renders `src/DcaShop.Web/Views/Product/Detail.cshtml`. All five scenarios show up in that page: the breadcrumb, the heading, the image, the description, the category, the \"Back to Products\" link, and the tab title (set through the layout's `<title>`). The seeded products the scenarios name are in `SampleDataSeeder.cs:25,26,32`.\n\n**Test levels:**\n- `view-details-opens-the-product-page` is the happy path, so it gets a Playwright browser test.\n- The other four get integration tests through `WebApplicationFactory`.\n\n**Coverage today:** four scenarios have no test at all.\n- **Happy path:** tests do click \"View Details\", but only by position, and none of them checks \"Domain-Driven Design\" or its heading.\n- **Image, description and category:** only the image is checked, and only partly: `HomeSliderE2eTest` compares the page's image with the slider card's. Nothing checks the description or the category.\n- **Tab title, breadcrumb and \"Back to Products\":** no test at all. The page object has a `BackToCatalogAsync` helper, but no test calls it.\n\n**Other points:**\n- No decision is needed from you, and no structural question came up. The designed and generated context maps agree on Product.\n- `dca-knowledge` wasn't consulted: adopting existing behaviour raised no pattern question.\n- The plan leaves two things to the test stage:\n  - whether an adopted story gets new tests for the scenarios nothing covers;\n  - whether the shared specification's `scenarios.md` needs a matching title for the happy path.\n- I didn't read the inventory the story's notes point to (P6, P7), because it isn't one of this stage's inputs.","ttft_ms":2676,"type":"result","duration_ms":92421,"uuid":"9acd71c6-0bfa-4019-856f-3d96b81b0878","ttft_stream_ms":1601,"time_to_request_ms":75,"first_content_frame_ms":1601,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
